sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Agent code
    participant P as pydantic_ai._step / openai _step_async
    participant V as decide_with_validation
    participant G as gate_async
    participant C as AsyncioChannel
    participant App as Approver
    participant Cursor as respond_or_forward

    Note over A,Cursor: Setup: same as the APPROVE flow — INTERACTIVE + channel attached.

    Note over A,Cursor: Stage 1 developer rewrites the outbound messages
    A->>P: await model.request(messages)
    P->>G: await gate_async(session, step)
    G->>C: await channel.submit(step)
    C->>App: pending step surfaced
    Note right of App: developer edits messages + model
    App->>C: channel.decide(EDIT(messages=[...], model=gpt-5))
    C->>V: decide_with_validation(decision)
    alt EDIT carries no override field
        V-->>C: raise ValueError
        Note right of V: fast-fail at the channel boundary
    else EDIT has at least one override
        V-->>C: validated Decision
    end
    C-->>G: Decision(kind=EDIT, messages, model)
    G-->>P: decision

    Note over A,Cursor: Stage 2 apply the edit before dispatch
    P->>P: messages = decision.messages<br/>kwargs.model = decision.model
    Note right of P: signature recomputed on the EDITED payload
    P->>Cursor: respond_or_forward(edited_signature)

    Note over A,Cursor: Stage 3 edited signature almost always diverges
    alt edited signature still matches recorded (rare — same hash by accident)
        Cursor-->>P: cached RecordedResponse
    else edited signature diverges (the common case)
        Cursor-->>P: None
        Note right of Cursor: BRANCH-like forward authorised
        P->>P: forward to live model with edited kwargs
        P->>P: capture live span under session.branch_id
    end
    P-->>A: edited response

    Note over A,Cursor: Stage 4 alternative — STOP unwinds the run
    alt developer chooses STOP instead
        App->>C: channel.decide(STOP)
        C-->>G: Decision(kind=STOP)
        G-->>P: decision(kind=STOP)
        P->>P: raise SteppingStopped(step)
        Note right of P: distinct from ReplayError —<br/>normal termination, not a contract violation
        P-->>A: SteppingStopped propagates<br/>(Phase B runner will catch → status=done)
    end

    Note over A,Cursor: Outcome: edit applied pre-dispatch; divergence is the expected path, not an error.
